Using energy conservation: \(e\Delta V=\frac12 m_e v^2\)

\[
v=\sqrt{\frac{2e\Delta V}{m_e}}
=\sqrt{\frac{2(1.602\times10^{-19})(25000)}{9.11\times10^{-31}}}
\approx 9.4\times10^7\ \text{m/s}
\]

Closest option: \(95{,}000{,}000\ \text{m/s}\).

Answer: G

For two masses connected by a spring, the relative motion has reduced mass

\[
\mu=\frac{m_1m_2}{m_1+m_2}
=\frac{(0.1)(0.2)}{0.3}
=\frac{1}{15}\text{ kg}.
\]

The angular frequency is

\[
\omega=\sqrt{\frac{k}{\mu}}
=\sqrt{\frac{0.5}{1/15}}
=\sqrt{7.5}\approx 2.74\ \text{rad s}^{-1}.
\]

